  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_snhunt",
      "name": {
        "en": "Snow Hunter's Badge",
        "zh": "雪猎证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_snhunt",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Snow Hunter has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for storing and unleashing capacitance-based firepower to penetrative ends when facing the enemy.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Sniper Operator during field operations to exercise Hunter responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员雪猎擅长蓄积火力对敌人进行贯穿打击\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为狙击干员，行使猎手职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_snhunt",
      "name": {
        "en": "Hunts of the Past",
        "zh": "过去的狩猎",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_snhunt",
      "description": {
        "en": "'When's Sir Arctosz gonna give us new hunting gear? Hey, Joanna, still using that spring trap your old man gave you a while back? How's the hunting lately, getting enough to eat?'\n'Joanna's twice the hunter you are. She's perfectly fine using older traps and crossbows. You need to train harder, not hope for shiny new contraptions.'\n'Well, what d'you want me to do? If I started training right now until I'm as good as her, all the animals on the mountain would've run off already, and all that training would go to waste.'\n'The railroad construction shouldn't affect the forest for too much longer... Hmm, have you considered moving down the mountain? I heard old Hans followed his son and daughter-in-law to the city recently.'\nThe villagers chatter away about the rumblings of the trains through the forest, the long level roads and the many marketplaces those roads connect to. Joanna sits to the side, adjusting her old spring trap. There are dark, minute gouges between its iron teeth thanks to many years of use, but its clasp remains nimble. She does not speak, simply retightening the trap in silence. She uses her fingertips to push down on the spring, ensuring its jaws still mesh together. Soon, she waves goodbye to the villagers as she begins today's hunt.\nThe sky is darkening, and a narrow hollow mars the vast snowfield, a shivering cloudbeast reclining within. The trap is not far, so it was most likely lured over by the scent of bait. A cloudbeast this young should not be out alone like this. Its fur has not yet lengthened, and its claws lack the length and strength to grasp. It must have wandered off from its kin. It tries to move forward, but the frigid wind forces it to curl up even tighter.\nJoanna crouches down, packing up the trap. She makes no move to capture the young beast, instead taking out some jerky and breaking off a small piece to gently place on the ground. She knows that with no one to care for this cloudbeast, it will not survive the cold night. She looks at the trembling beastling, a complex bitterness welling up in her chest.\nHas Dad come back from the train station yet? A thought suddenly comes to Joanna. Maybe one day, her family will move down the mountain too. Maybe one day, her dad will agree to work at the crafting hall, where he can keep carving statues of Kjeragandr in a workshop... Kjeragandr's body stands as tall as ever, the endless freezing winds whistling past as they always have, and the spring trap her dad gave her still works great. It's not like everyone really needs new tools or a new place to be. Why does it feel like the more the land moves forward, the less people can actually hold onto? Joanna cradles the beastling, tucking it inside her jacket. It snuggles against her, the tips of its fur dripping with melted snow. The touch of cold water against her chest jolts her. She looks down at the weak cloudbeast. It seems to have settled down a little.\n'Let's leave it for tomorrow. I'll go hunting with everyone then. There's always a way.' A faint pulse beats against Joanna's chest. The snowy path under her stretches on in peaceful silence.",
        "zh": "“阿克托斯老爷什么时候给我们分发新的狩猎工具啊？哎，茱安娜，你还在用你爸当年给你做的这个弹簧陷阱啊，最近怎么样，每次猎到的东西够吃吗？”\n“茱安娜的技术可比你好了不知道多少倍，人家用老式陷阱和旧的弩箭也能猎到猎物，你还是再好好练练吧，别老是指望用什么新武器。”\n“那你说怎么办？我从现在开始练，练到和茱安娜一样厉害了，山上的动物早就跑没了，练了也没用啊。”\n“修路通列车对雪林的影响应该不会持续太久吧……不过，是不是也可以考虑搬到山下呢？我听说老汉斯最近就跟着他儿子儿媳搬到城里去了。”\n乡亲们还在你一言我一语地谈论着雪林中出现的列车轰鸣、绵延而去的平坦道路以及道路连接起来的一个又一个闹市。茱安娜在一旁调试着自己的老式弹簧陷阱。这么多年过去，铁齿间已产生了细小的沟壑般的暗色痕迹，但卡扣依然灵活。她没有插话，只是默默把陷阱重新收紧，又用指尖推了推弹簧，确认它仍能咬合，随后跟老乡们挥了挥手道别，开始了今天的狩猎工作。\n天色渐晚，白茫茫的雪中凹出窄窄的一道印记，里面躺着一只瑟瑟发抖的云兽。陷阱就在不远处，它大概是被陷阱中食物的气味吸引来的。这样小的云兽不该独自出现在这里，它的绒毛还没长齐，爪子细小无力，显然是和同类走散了。它试图往前挪，却被冷风逼得缩成一团。\n茱安娜蹲下身，先把陷阱收了起来。她没有去抓那只小兽，而是拿出随身携带的肉干掰下一小块，轻轻放在雪地上。她知道，这样的云兽要是没人管，今晚恐怕就熬不过去。她望着小兽颤抖的身影，心里涌起一种复杂的酸涩。\n不知道爸爸从车站回来了没有？茱安娜突然想到，也许有一天自己家也会搬去山下，也许有一天爸爸会答应工艺厂的人，去车间里继续雕刻耶拉冈德的神像……耶拉冈德的身躯依旧挺立着，经年不息的风雪依旧呼啸而过，爸爸给自己做的弹簧陷阱也依旧很好用，也许不是每个人都非要拥有新的工具、新的环境，为什么世事好像总是在往前赶，大家手里能抓住的东西却越来越少？茱安娜抱起小兽，把它揣进衣襟里，小兽在她怀里轻轻蹭动，毛尖带着雪水，凉得她胸口一紧。她低头看向瘦弱的小兽，它的动作不自觉放缓了几分。\n“明天再继续吧，明天再和大家一起来狩猎，总会有办法的。”茱安娜的怀里传来微弱的心跳，脚下的雪路安静而漫长。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
